NOTABLE_GAPS:
Empty or thin cells. Opus postumum: only Howard (2019); S2 and CrossRef searches found no 2020 or 2021 Opus postumum item beyond a chapter and low-cited papers (for example, the fascicle XI chapter in Force and Understanding, 2021, with one S2 citation). Pre-critical work: covered only as a secondary tag (Abaci and Fugate 2019, Allison 2020); no 2021 pre-critical item was verified. Education and pedagogy: none in any year (Formosa, 'A Kantian approach to education for moral sensitivity', Journal of Philosophy of Education 2021, and Sticker and Bakhurst's special-issue introduction were screened out on the per-year cap). Animals: only Allais and Callanan (2020); Browning on animal minds (Kantian Review 2021) was screened out. Edition and translation: only the 2019 Yale Groundwork; no new Cambridge Edition volume or translation for 2020 or 2021 was found, the 2021 De Gruyter record of the Kant-Lexikon appears to be a reissue of the 2015 work already in Domain 2, and Guyer and Wood's Introducing Kant's Critique of Pure Reason (2021) is a Cambridge Element. Metaphysics of Morals and virtue: no 2021 monograph (Timmons, Kant's Doctrine of Virtue, has CrossRef print year 2022; Kahn on conscience is a 2021 Cambridge Element and was screened out). Reception: no neo-Kantian or phenomenological entry for 2019 or 2021 beyond Schulting and Ameriks (the 2021 Pendlebury PPR article has CrossRef print year 2022); Brandom's Hegel book (2019) was excluded as not Kant-central. Logic: Lapointe (ed.), Logic from Kant to Russell (2019), was found and screened out. Race in 2021: the only entry is Yab's book, with no retrievable abstract (INCOMPLETE); Lu-Adler's article on travel reports and race has CrossRef print date 2022-02 and belongs to the next block. NDPR coverage: reviews were found for Watkins (2019), Abaci (2019), Ameriks (2019), Allison (2020) and Kraus (2020), but searches returned no NDPR review for any 2021 entry (only non-matching reviews), so 2021 review evidence comes from Kantian Review, Mind, Philosophical Review, JHP, PQ, EJP, AGPh and Kant-Studien reviews listed in each note. Citation counts for 2021 works are small (S2 and CrossRef counts of 1 to 36), so significance for 2021 rests on publisher, venue and review coverage as much as on citations.
